{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789492470,"nonce":"O4NWX1hpG6wQIx9GeLtRlWstqAU=","message":"Root-cause analysis\n-------------------\n\nCode path\n~~~~~~~~~\n\nSearch requests reach the network through:\n\n- ``get_pi_search_results()`` -- ``src/b4/__init__.py:4341-4363``. Calls\n  ``node.get_mbox_by_query(query, full_threads=..., nocache=...)``. It reads\n  no config of its own; the only config-derived value it touches is\n  ``node.hostname``, used for the log line.\n- ``get_lore_node()`` -- ``src/b4/__init__.py:4185-4216``. Builds the\n  singleton ``LoreNode``. The base URL comes solely from ``b4.midmask``\n  (line 4197), stripped of ``/%s`` (line 4199), with ``/all`` appended when\n  the mask carried no list path (lines 4201-4205).\n- ``LoreNode.get_mbox_by_query()`` -- ``liblore/src/liblore/node.py:1020-1024``.\n  Composes the URL itself:\n  ``self._url + '/?x=m' + t_param + '\u0026q=' + quote_plus(query)``, where\n  ``t_param`` is ``'\u0026t=1'`` when ``full_threads`` is set.\n\n``self._url`` is the base passed by ``get_lore_node()``, so the search\norigin and path are a function of ``b4.midmask`` alone.\n\nWhere it breaks\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nThe read of the setting was removed in db4cd69. Before that commit,\n``get_pi_search_results()`` contained the full implementation at\n``db4cd69^:src/b4/__init__.py:3815-3827``:\n\n- line 3815: ``searchmask = config.get('searchmask')``\n- lines 3816-3821: absent or non-string value was a fatal error\n- lines 3822-3824: ``\u0026t=1`` appended when ``full_threads`` and not already\n  present in the mask\n- line 3827: ``query_url = searchmask % query``\n\nSo the setting was the entire URL template, not a component of one. Nothing\nequivalent survives in the current code.\n\nCauses\n~~~~~~\n\n1. The migration swapped a caller-supplied URL template for a URL that\n   liblore composes from a base, and the base was wired to ``b4.midmask``.\n   That silently narrowed the setting's expressiveness from \"any search URL\"\n   to \"the midmask origin with a fixed query shape\".\n2. liblore offers no place to put it. ``LoreNode.from_git_config()``\n   (``liblore/src/liblore/node.py:275-305``) documents ``fallback``,\n   ``autoprobe``, ``probetimeout`` and ``probettl``. There is no search-URL\n   or query-template parameter, so ``get_lore_node()`` has nothing to pass a\n   ``searchmask`` into.\n3. The orphaned setting stayed in ``DEFAULT_CONFIG`` and in\n   ``docs/config.rst``, so neither the code nor the docs flagged it as dead,\n   and no warning path exists for a user who has it set.\n\nProven vs. inferred\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nProven by reading code: that no ``src/b4/`` path reads ``b4.searchmask``\n(tree-wide grep finds it only in ``docs/config.rst``); that the search URL\nis composed from the midmask-derived base; that liblore's config surface has\nno search-URL key; and that the old default mask is byte-identical to what\nliblore now composes, which is why defaults-only users see no difference.\n\nNot verified at runtime: no b4 command was executed for this analysis, so\nthe user-visible symptom is predicted from the code path rather than\nobserved.\n\nRelated\n~~~~~~~\n\n- a0c4ddb (closed) -- also fallout from the liblore migration, but a\n  different mechanism (a pinned liblore missing ``reset_cancel()``).\n- 4c18c1c -- unrelated mechanism, shares the ``b4 config:`` component.","files":null}]}